      <h2 class="block-title">Multi-Configuration Scaling: Microarchitectural Tuning Impact</h2>
      <p class="block-lead">
        A 64-bit application core is not a static point in design space—it is an extensible silicon generator. Parametric switches—such as expanding superscalar issue width from 1-wide to 4-wide, doubling L1 cache depth, adding non-blocking MSHR registers, or scaling from a single core to an 8-tile coherent mesh—dramatically reshape performance, clock frequency, and silicon gate count.
